    quest.4B0A3CBC172501F6.title: "Brain of Cthulhu Respawn Cage"
    quest.4B0B81F46A5AA9B1.quest_desc: [
        " An exquisitely crafted lamp. Its color suggests it might be cast from bronze, yet it bears no trace of verdigris; I suspect its material is some kind of magic-infused metal."
        " The ancient lamp may have lain dormant underground for centuries. As I picked it up, I felt a lingering warmth in my palm, as if its flame had been extinguished not long ago."
        " For what purpose was it forged? Perhaps before its power fades with the passing ages, the flame from this lantern could turn a forest into a sea of fire. However, its appearance hardly suggests a weapon... It seems more likely its original and current purpose is to clear thorns."
        " Someone left it here for those who came after. Whether that person was a previous explorer or the original inhabitant of this place, I have no way of knowing. They left a key, allowing later comers to follow in their footsteps and obtain evidence of a once-glorious civilization's existence."
        " I stood again before the thorn thicket. The lamp, with only embers left, exhaled a faint flame. The moment the sparks touched the thorns, these plants, which axes and swords could not harm, were instantly consumed, shattering to dust before my boots."
        " I stepped over them, carrying the lamp towards the desolate castle, where the forgotten perhaps lie buried."
    ]
    quest.4B0B81F46A5AA9B1.quest_subtitle: "An oil lamp of unknown material, which I found inside a troll cave."
    quest.4B0B81F46A5AA9B1.title: "&5The magical flame within it has the power I imagined to clear the Highland Thorns."
    quest.4B2A79FC0C011CB2.quest_desc: [
        "&aObjective: Collect the Dragonsteel Forge Cores and successfully build the Dragonsteel Forge."
        "{ \"text\": \"Complete Main Quest Chapter III to receive Dragonsteel Forge materials. Click to jump.\", \"underlined\": true, \"color\": green, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"6344D6B5AEC69478\" } }"
        ""
        "&eThe Dragonsteel Forge &6is a &amultiblock structure &6used to forge Dragonsteel."
        "&6Please refer to the Dragonsteel Forge chapter in the &eBestiary &6for construction methods."
        "&6The recipes for Dragonsteel and Ancient Dragon Heart in this modpack have been modified:"
        ""
        "&cThermal Springstone Ingot + Fire Dragon Blood = Dragonsteel (Dragon Forge)"
        "&bPermafrost Ingot + Ice Dragon Blood = Dragonsteel (Dragon Forge)"
        "&dAether Ingot + Lightning Dragon Blood = Dragonsteel (Dragon Forge)"
        "&eNetherite Ingot + Frail Dragon Heart = Ancient Dragon Heart (Any Dragonsteel Forge)"
        ""
        "&6Additionally, &aa player-turned-dragon &6can also breathe &dDragonbreath &6to use the Dragonsteel Forge,"
        "&6without being limited by the dragon's type or the forge's type."
    ]
    quest.4B2A79FC0C011CB2.quest_subtitle: "Special Dragonsteel Recipes"
    quest.4B2A79FC0C011CB2.title: "Dragonsteel Forge"
    quest.4BCF83DBB5612B54.quest_subtitle: "Guaranteed once per dragon"
    quest.4BCF83DBB5612B54.title: "Doppelganger Ring Guarantee"
    quest.4BD6C7A2A6DC392B.quest_desc: [
        "&aObjective: Obtain a Dehydrated Ghast"
        ""
        "&6Dehydrated Ghasts can sometimes be found near &ffossils &6in the Nether."
        "&6After being placed in water for about &220 minutes&6, a Dehydrated Ghast will transform into a &6Ghastling&6. After another &220 minutes&6, it will grow into a &6Happy Ghast&6."
        "&6Feeding a &rSnowball &6to a Ghastling can speed up its growth."
        "&6Players can use a &dHarness &6on a Happy Ghast to make it rideable,"
        "&6and use shears to remove the harness when not riding."
        ""
        "&7&oNaming it \"kiki\" yields a surprise."
    ]
    quest.4BE17AD8808CFFEF.quest_desc: [
        "&6The Scroll Scribing Table &ris used to scribe various &eSpell Scrolls&r."
        ""
        "Spell scroll recipes can be viewed by searching &aEMI &rfor \"scroll\"."
        ""
        "1. Place &dInk&r. The quality of the ink determines the scroll's quality."
        ""
        "2. Place &dPaper&r. Scribing a scroll consumes one piece of paper."
        ""
        "3. Place &dFocuses&r. Focuses determine the spell's school."
        ""
        "4. After placing Focuses, the scribable spells will be displayed."
        ""
        "&o&7Some spells may show as question marks. Try using higher quality ink."
    ]
    quest.4BE17AD8808CFFEF.quest_subtitle: "Scribe Your Legend"
